   "note": "Matt's tall-chain layout reworked (2026-11-14): rx_t as laid out (chain + one-row log_det_t, unflipped: input at the west end, flowing east), RX on ua[2] / ua[1] so the input section sits bottom-left, TX drivers on their own pads ua[3] / ua[4] in the strip west of it (TX is off in RX, so no isolation needed), dbg moves to ua[5]. det comes out at the detector's west end: LPF, averager, comparator, Ctrim and the trim DAC run east along the top towards the macro. Everything but the macro shifted 15 um west (bias 21 um from the macro halo; the RX inputs run ~15 um west along the bottom from ua[2] / ua[1] to the chain). Bias east of the chain's output end (ib_chain / vcm run west along the bottom to the chain's south-edge pins). Pinout change: rx ua[0]/ua[1] -> ua[2]/ua[1], dbg ua[2] -> ua[5]. Rule 2's 4 um is the flyline of o4 past stage 1; the real taps are wired in rx_t's channel (PEX: nothing back to the input).",
